# BUGS

A heap holds one mapping for each 256 MiB it has grown to, of a task's 85, so it reaches its 16 GiB only in a task with few other mappings; a task's memory budget (09's `vx_mem_budget`) does not size it yet.

A small block's free list is kept in the freed blocks themselves, so a write after a free can corrupt the heap rather than fault.
